        {
          "say": "Three thousand four hundred is ambiguous. Scientific notation fixes it.",
          "write": "3.40 × 10³ → 3 sig figs"
        },
        {
          "say": "Exact numbers, like 5 test tubes, never limit your answer.",
          "write": "exact numbers: unlimited"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The two rules",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Times and divide: count the digits.",
          "write": "× ÷ → fewest sig figs"
        },
        {
          "say": "2.5 times 3.142 is 7.855. Round to 2 sig figs: 7.9.",
          "write": "2.5 × 3.142 = 7.9"
        },
        {
          "say": "Add and subtract: count the decimal places.",
          "write": "+ − → fewest decimal places"
        },
        {
          "say": "105.2 plus 0.346 is 105.546. Round to one decimal place.",
          "write": "105.2 + 0.346 = 105.5",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 290,
            "alt": "Decimal places",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 400,
                "y": 80,
                "text": "105.2",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "end",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 400,
                "y": 130,
                "text": "+   0.346",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "end",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "line",
                "x": 200,
                "y": 150,
                "x2": 420,
                "y2": 150,
                "color": "black"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 400,
                "y": 200,
                "text": "105.546",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "end",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 400,
                "y": 260,
                "text": "105.5",
                "size": 30,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "end",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Round only once, at the very end.",
          "write": "round once, at the end"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Units and prefixes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "A prefix multiplies a unit by a power of ten.",
          "write": "prefix = power of ten"
        },
        {
          "say": "Kilo is 10 to the 3. Milli is 10 to the minus 3.",
          "write": "k 10³   m 10⁻³   μ 10⁻⁶"
        },
        {
          "say": "One litre is 1000 millilitres. So 250 millilitres is 0.250 litres.",
          "write": "250 mL = 0.250 L",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "mL to L",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 40,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "250 mL"
              },
              {
                "kind": "arrow",
                "x": 230,
                "y": 140,
                "x2": 330,
                "y2": 140,
                "color": "purple",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 340,
                "y": 100,
                "w": 180,
                "h": 80,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "0.250 L",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 120,
                "text": "÷ 1000",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Small to big, the number gets big. Big to small, it shrinks.",
          "write": "L → mL: × 1000"
        },
        {
          "say": "Kelvin is degrees Celsius plus 273.",
          "write": "T(K) = T(°C) + 273"
        },
        {
          "say": "One atmosphere is 101.325 kilopascals.",
          "write": "1 atm = 101.325 kPa"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "A full calculation",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Dissolve 5.00 grams of salt to make 250.0 millilitres of solution.",
          "write": "5.00 g NaCl in 250.0 mL"
        },
        {
          "say": "Use data book values. Sodium chloride is 58.5.",
          "write": "M = 23.0 + 35.5 = 58.5"
        },
        {
          "say": "n equals 5.00 over 58.5. Keep every digit.",
          "write": "n = 0.085470… mol"
        },
        {
          "say": "Convert the volume first. 250.0 millilitres is 0.2500 litres.",
          "write": "V = 0.2500 L"
        },
        {
          "say": "c equals n over V. That gives 0.342 moles per litre, 3 sig figs.",
          "write": "c = 0.342 mol L⁻¹",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 300,
            "alt": "Sig figs in the data",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "5.00 (3)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 200,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "58.5 (3)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 380,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 160,
                "h": 70,
                "fill": "teal",
                "label": "0.2500 (4)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 280,
                "y": 230,
                "text": "answer: 3 sig figs",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "purple",
                "anchor": "middle",
                "bold": true,
                "change": "add"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Rounding n early to 0.09 gives 0.36. That is about 5 percent too high.",
          "write": "✗ 0.36 if rounded early"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The data book",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The data book is provided in every test and the exam.",
          "write": "data book"
        },
        {
          "say": "It has relative atomic masses, constants, and key formulas.",
          "write": "Nₐ = 6.02 × 10²³ mol⁻¹"
        },
        {
          "say": "Always use its values, like sodium 23.0 and chlorine 35.5.",
          "write": "Na 23.0   Cl 35.5"
        },
        {
          "say": "Learn its layout early, so you find things in seconds.",
          "write": "know the layout"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Remember",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Times and divide, count digits. Add and subtract, count decimals.",
          "write": "digits vs decimals"
        },
        {
          "say": "Leading zeros never count. Sandwich zeros always count.",
          "write": "0.0052 → 2 sig figs"
        },
        {
          "say": "Did you turn millilitres into litres?",
          "write": "mL → L?"
        },
        {
          "say": "Keep every digit until the last line, then round once.",
          "write": "round once"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}